# Onboarding revamp brainstorm

Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 11:02 · 29 min

## Attendees

- Noor Haddad
- Shreyas
- Tom Becker
- Priya Nair

## Notes

#### Decisions

- The top three onboarding ideas from the dot vote are CSV import, a guided setup checklist (with an internal stuck-customer view for Tom), and admin-consent bulk calendar connect.
- The in-app chat widget is rejected because of the support load it would put on Tom.
- CSV import v1 covers technicians only; job import waits until Priya's threat model is done.
- CSV import will parse server-side with a 5,000-row / 5 MB cap, accept CSV only (no Excel), import allow-listed columns only, delete raw uploads after 24 hours, and escape formula-leading characters on export.
- Admin-consent calendar connect is designed now but built only after the Calendar Sync v2 beta (13 November), without pulling in Maya before then.
- Templates per trade and the sample-data sandbox are parked for later, not built this quarter.
- Interim target of 10 days to first dispatch for customers onboarded in October and November; 7 days is the target once admin-consent connect ships.
- The under-seven-days target is measured in calendar days.

#### Key facts

- **What is the interim time-to-first-dispatch target before admin consent ships?** Ten days for customers onboarded in October and November; seven days once admin-consent calendar connect ships.
- **How long does it currently take a new customer to reach their first dispatch, and what is the target?** About 19 days today (Tom's figure from memory); the goal is under 7 days.
- **How is first dispatch defined?** The first job a dispatcher assigns to a real technician that the technician actually opens on the mobile app; test jobs and kickoff-call jobs don't count.
- **How long did Fernhollow spend waiting on technicians to connect their calendars?** Eleven days.
- **Why was the in-app chat widget rejected?** Support load: Tom is the only support engineer, ticket volume is up about 40% since the sync bug, and a chat widget with nobody behind it is worse than none.
- **What were the dot-vote results?** CSV import 4 dots, setup checklist 3, admin-consent calendar connect 3, templates per trade 1, sandbox 1, white-glove week 0.
- **What size limits were agreed for the CSV import?** 5,000 rows and 5 MB per file, CSV only (no Excel files).
- **What three security concerns did Priya raise about CSV import?** PII (personal phone numbers, home addresses, end-customer addresses and gate codes), unbounded file size, and formula injection when data is exported and opened in Excel.
- **Why won't admin-consent calendar connect be built until after 13 November?** It sits next to Calendar Sync v2, and Shreyas doesn't want to put it on Maya until after the v2 beta on 13 November.
- **When is the follow-up review?** Tuesday 13 October 2026, with the same four people, not in the Blue room.

